A||N||4||MR2KLR||What injector is best?(2.5L)||||1||
Z||000000||MR2KLR||12-01-2001||01:18 PM||||<BR>I got three used injectors from work to day one from a 2.0L OHC Sunbird another from a 2.0L OHC Cavalier and the 3rd from a Skylark with a DIS 2.5L Duke. I instaled the Skylark injector and the car now runs. Would either of the others work better? anybody know the LBS? or anything like that? my interchange book says that they are diffrent. but they all mount the same and look the same I asume the diff. is  the LB/HR. rates<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-01-2001||03:31 PM||||If you look, the smaller motors likely have smaller bore TBI....<P>I'm guessing you've got a DIS 2.5.....<P>At normal run the injectors likely won't matter much. The ECM will just adjust the injector timing to add fuel as needed. at least within a certain range....<P>Where you could have trouble is at WOT. you could run lean which would not be good for the motor.<P>I'd put the one from the other 2.5 in it. That should be allot closer if not identical.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||erikred||12-03-2001||11:07 AM||||What color are the injectors. I have a print out from a web site that tells the flow rate according to the color.<P>Erik-||||reg||1
Z||000003||MR2KLR||12-03-2001||09:10 PM||||The one from the 2.0L Sunbird is white/yellowish the 2.0L cavalier is lt. brown and so is the 2.5L Skylark.<P>Both of the 2.0L injectors have a diffrent top O-ring I will try the 2.5L O-ring on the Sunbird injector only if it flows better the skylark injector (the one i'm useing for now) is very loud (buzzing), I think it's going to fail soon.<P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||erikred||12-04-2001||11:48 AM||||Go her for the chart <A HREF="http://www.diy-efi.org/gmecm/component_info/tbi_injectors.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.diy-efi.org/gmecm/component_info/tbi_injectors.html</A> <P>There are two color codes painted on the metal knob that is between the two electric terminals on top of the injector. You will see this in the picture.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Erik-||||reg||7
